group tooling
note Rust sources as tree-sitter syntax trees, for archlint and the API lock. The walk takes every file under the root the way git sees it (ignore files honoured, hidden files included, .git, .jj, target and the cache skipped), and the Rust files under crates/ and xtask/ are what is linted. A SourceFile is its path, text, tree and zone. The helpers walk the tree without name resolution: everything a rule decides, it decides from syntax and the file's path.

